stead of praying at altars (which might not be encountered or might have wrong alignment), let me modify my change to be more broadly effective.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the entire approach. The fact that the score didn't change means my hypothesis was wrong or the implementation didn't work as expected. Let me think of a different focused change.\n\nPossible alternatives:\n1. **Elbereth engraving improvement**: Make the bot engrave Elbereth earlier and more reliably\n2. **Better early game combat**: Avoid fighting monsters without Elbereth\n3. **Potion identification by reading**: Make the bot read unidentified potions to identify them (not just at altars)\n4. **Never quaff unidentified potions**: Simply add a check to avoid drinking unidentified potions in last resort\n\nLet me try a different change. Actually, let me first understand why the results are identical. Maybe I should check if the altar encounter happened.\n\nActually, let me take a step back. The evaluation gives the same per-seed results, which means the bot plays out the exact same game with the same deaths. This makes sense because:\n- The seed determines everything (dungeon layout, monster generation, item generation)\n- My change only adds a prayer step at altars\n- If the bot never encounters an altar before dying, or the altar alignment is wrong, the game plays out identically\n\nSo my change didn't help because the 3 early-death seeds don't encounter compatible altars before dying. I need a different approach.\n\nLet me think of a different focused change that would more reliably help.\n\n**New hypothesis**: **Making the bot engrave Elbereth at the start of every game** will prevent early melee deaths (ogre, rothe) by keeping monsters at bay. This would help the bot survive to higher XL and deeper levels.\n\nLet me implement this. The change would be:\n1. In the agent's first steps, engrave \"Elbereth\" on the floor\n2. This engraving will respect Elbereth, causing most monsters to not attack the bot\n\nThis is a single coherent idea (Elbereth engraving at start), and it should help with the ogre/rothe deaths at Xp:7.\n\nActually, wait. The bot might already engrave Elbereth as part of its normal play. Let me check if Elbereth engraving is already happening.\n\nLooking at the code, the `elbereth_rest` strategy in `dive_logic.py` handles Elbereth resting during the dive phase. But during the early tour/leveling phase, I'm not sure if Elbereth is engraved.\n\nLet me check the exploration code for Elbereth engraving.\n\nActually, let me just try the Elbereth engraving change. I'll add code to engrave Elbereth at the start of the game, which should provide early-game survival benefit.\n\nBut I need to be careful - engraving Elbereth takes a turn, and if done incorrectly, it could waste time. Also, engraving Elbereth while a monster is adjacent could be dangerous.\n\nLet me look at how engraving works in the code.","time":{"start":1790511447143,"end":1790511494478}}}
